    {
      "slug": "gismonda",
      "title": "Gismonda",
      "year": 1894,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Mucha_-_Gismonda.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 1267,
      "imageHeight": 3422,
      "story": "Gismonda is a Greek-set melodrama in four acts by Victorien Sardou that premiered on October 31, 1894 at the Théâtre de la Renaissance. In 1918, the play was adapted for the now lost film Love's Conquest. In 1918/1919, it was adapted into the opera Gismonda by Henry Février.",
      "facts": [
        "In the opening act, we find Gismonda, the widow of the Duke of Athens, and the mother of his child, a five-year-old boy named Francesco.",
        "Gismonda is the ruling power of the duchy as regent for her son, an absolute monarch."
      ],
